# Feedback loop design

Feedback loop design is the practice of systematically improving efficiency and output. It involves identifying and implementing methods, techniques, and frameworks that maximize personal or organizational productivity while maintaining sustainable work practices.

This skill is primarily discussed in a single source, offering a focused perspective on its application.
